[38;2;124;124;124mP(x) is always false).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe question is whether adding the empty domain to the semantics makes the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mmonadic fragment undecidable.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this. In inclusive logic:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- ∀x φ is vacuously true in the empty domain[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- ∃x φ is vacuously false in the empty domain[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the empty domain is a specific model. The satisfiability problem for [0m
[38;2;124;124;124minclusive monadic logic asks: is there a model (possibly with empty domain) [0m
